# ChatBI Governance crontab - portable template (operator adapts to real infra)
#
# This is a PORTABLE schedule specification, NOT a runnable crontab as-is. The
# harness ships NO scheduler and does NOT assume a resident Agent (FR-2 non-goal:
# docs/requirements-proactive-governance.md:138). Entries below are interactive
# Claude Code slash commands (harness/.claude/commands/) that cron cannot invoke
# directly. Adapt each entry to your real scheduling infrastructure (cron, Airflow,
# k8s CronJob, systemd timer). See docs/harness/scheduling.md.
#
# Two environment variables MUST be set by the operator before any entry runs:
#   CHATBI_WORKSPACE  absolute path to the Warehouse Workspace root
#   CHATBI_INVOKE     how your infra triggers a governance slash command
#                     (e.g. 'claude -p' is a CANDIDATE, operator-verified; the
#                     harness does NOT guarantee a headless invocation path)
# Unset -> the ${VAR:?} expansion fails loud (HOOK-004 fail-closed); the entry
# does NOT run silently.
#
# PORT-001: this file MUST contain no machine paths. It is guarded by
# chatbi_harness.schedules.validate_crontab_portability (unit tests + build) and
# the build-product.sh canary sweep. Do NOT edit a machine path into this file;
# set CHATBI_WORKSPACE in your infra instead.
#
# Evidence: only /chatbi-audit-drift persists to .chatbi/runs/<sid>/ today
# (drift_report.json). The other activities return results in the chat footer
# only; persisting them to .chatbi/runs/ is a follow-up (out of crontab-config-
# only scope). Each entry's evidence expectation is noted inline.
#
# Cadence: daily = drift accumulates fast (FM-STALE); weekly = periodic
# refresh/regression (META-005, FBK-001); on-change = event-driven (no cron line,
# wire to your infra's event trigger).
#
# Human-protection: every activity only DRAFTS candidates; all merges still
# require domain-owner approval (SEM-003/FBK-002). The harness connects to no
# external communication system by default (requirements §8 out-of-scope).

SHELL=/bin/sh

# daily: proactive drift audit (FR-1) | evidence: drift_report.json -> .chatbi/runs/<sid>/ (HAS write_state)
0 1 * * * cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-audit-drift --scope all

# weekly: reference refresh, draft only (SEM-003) | evidence: no write_state today (chat footer); follow-up
0 2 * * 1 cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-maintain-knowledge

# weekly: model maintenance, draft only (SEM-003) | evidence: no write_state today (chat footer); follow-up
0 3 * * 1 cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-maintain-model

# weekly: evaluation regression (EVAL-001..004, FR-4 threshold) | evidence: no write_state today (chat footer); follow-up
0 4 * * 1 cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-evaluate

# on-change: correction review queue (FBK-001/002) - event-driven, no default cron line.
# Wire to your infra's event trigger, or uncomment for an optional weekly queue-drain:
# 0 5 * * 5 cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-correction

# optional weekly: readiness diagnostic (read-only, not a periodic-governance activity).
# Uncomment for a weekly health check after config changes:
# 0 6 * * 1 cd "${CHATBI_WORKSPACE:?}" && ${CHATBI_INVOKE:?} /chatbi-init
